{"kind":"assert","text":"H1 (71bb8559): items 1 to 6 and 8 are built at bb6e9128 on builder/h1-sequenced-level-20261113 (on main 324a0679, pushed). Item 7 waits for this ruling: no reason code is added. A TODO in packages/contract/src/read.ts names each code below.\n\nReason codes, each with a proposed RC-1 class:\n- `order-unavailable` (refusal, and `UnavailableReason`): never. The genesis pins the order reference and the order scope's kind for life.\n- `not-a-member` (refusal): head. An allocation asked before the creator's `enroll` lands succeeds after it.\n- `order-forming` (refusal): head. The group opens when its last member enrolls.\n- `cut-gone` (refusal of an act): head. A repeat takes a new position and can succeed.\n- `position-bound` (refusal of a resolve): never. A resolved allocation is final.\n- `not-open` (refusal of a resolve): never. That position always belongs to another member or input.\n- `allocation-expired` (refusal of a resolve): never. `expired` is final.\n- `holed` (refusal of a resolve): never. `holed` is final. Note section 5.3 uses it, and section 13.2 does not list it.\n- `source-not-effective` (delivery refusal): no class. It is a source check that records nothing, like `source-unverified`. As a `RefusalReason` it would be never.\n- `member-pending`, `member-uncommitted` (`UnavailableReason` only): no class. The turn ends unavailable and retries.\n- `uncommitted`, `cut-gone` as answers of the `at` read: kept only in `AtRead`. Question: do they join `ReadRefusal`?\n`order-left` and `order-closed` are not needed, because version 1 has no `leave` or `close`.\n\nChoices to confirm:\n1. `derivable` returns false for sequenced version 1, so creating a scope with one is still refused `unsupported-definition`. The head that derives the level removes this guard.\n2. The validator refuses each misuse with the existing `shape` code at its exact path. H1 adds no problem code.\n3. `ScopeApi.at` is not added. A required method breaks the Worker and